; Regression: a NAMESPACE function call with too many arguments used to compile
; clean (2026-08-15).
;
; The same silence as xfail_static_call_arity, reached through the other member
; container. A namespace's functions are members like a structure's, so
; `ns.greet(1, 2)` falls to the same s155 static path once the namespace-function
; branch above it has rejected the call on arity — and that branch's rejection
; was the whole mechanism by which the wrong call arrived at a path with no gate.
;
; Kept as a separate test from the structure case because the two travel through
; different `choose` arms when the member list is collected (Structure / Union /
; Namespace), and a gate that covers only the arm it was written against is the
; defect this file exists to catch.
;
; xfail: wrong number of arguments for ns.greet: got 2, expected 1

define ns
{
    function greet(a: int) returns int
    {
        a + 1
    }
}

let r ns.greet(1, 2)
print "unreachable"
